      "writtenOn": "2024-01-03T00:59:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this the debug_id from the C version. If so I would use the same name as it should not be used for any functional checks.\n\n(edit) I see that you refs_by_node tree in the C version by refs.by_global_id in this version. Is that needed? The node pointer allocated from the kernel heap is a guaranteed unique value that can never change for a live object. Can it not be used as the key in rust as well?",
      "revId": "c0bf3401d8ad68c748aa0c67ef2ed634bafbfd7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
